---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const description =
  "TreadGrade is an independent reference for NHTSA UTQG tire grades and DOT plant codes. It is not a tire seller and it is not a government site.";
const crumbs = [
  { href: "/", label: "Home" },
  { href: "/about/", label: "About" },
];
---

<Base title="About TreadGrade" description={description} breadcrumbs={crumbs}>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h1>About TreadGrade</h1>
    <p>
      TreadGrade is a reference for two public U.S. tire files: NHTSA's UTQG ratings, and NHTSA's tire plant codes. It is for someone comparing a grade molded on a sidewall, or reading the DOT code to see which plant and which manufacture week it names.
    </p>
    <p>
      It is not NHTSA, not the Department of Transportation, and not a tire dealer. It does not sell tires. It does not publish original tests, reviews, or prices. Grade and plant pages repeat the official records, with the preparation described on the <a href="/methodology/">data sources</a> page.
    </p>
    <p>
      If affiliate links are turned on later, they are labeled and disclosed. None are turned on in the default configuration. Sorts order the grades in NHTSA's list. They are not a ranking of the best tire, and they are not ordered by a commission.
    </p>
    <p><a href="/contact/">Contact</a> · <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> · <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Affiliate disclosure</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>
